            <div xml:id="d793">

                <pb facs="0984" n="970" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg970"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">103.9169: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-09T16:00:00-04:00">February 9, 1945—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>86. For Davis from Gardiner and Fraser FEA. Your 71, February 3. We wish you to
                    maintain position that USCCA is immune from suit and therefore not liable for
                    claims outlined in your cable, unless Embassy has strong objections.</p>
                <p>Following your full report, we will give consideration to union’s demand for
                    contract in accordance with your wishes. [Gardiner and Fraser.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
